  "title": "General Info: inst-comp-eeg",
  "description": "EEG dataset from an instruction-following study in which participants received novel verbal instructions combining integration or selection of animate and inanimate images, a relevant feature (color or shape), and a response key. Each participant completed a main instruction-following task and a 1-back localizer task in a single session. The dataset supports investigation of neural representations of novel instructions.",
  "methods_description": "Each participant was recorded in one session. In the main task, four sequential instruction screens (200 ms display, 800 ms interscreen interval) were followed by a pretarget interval and target images (200 ms). Participants judged whether the targets fulfilled the instruction. Catch trials were included. The main task had 16 blocks of 32 trials with fully counterbalanced conditions. The localizer was a 1-back subcategory task with 8 blocks of 40 trials. Block order was counterbalanced.",
